NATIVE BUILD AND SOURCE COMPOSITION VERIFICATION

2026-11-17. The latest native Linux and Windows/Wine builders generated all
43 artifacts from the canonical project and bootstrap/zero64.zapp. Every
artifact was byte-identical between the two hosts, including the compiler
fixed-point apps, BIOS/UEFI components, kernels, bundle, ISO and native tools.
The Windows builder was itself rebuilt by the original Zero compiler and ran
with no external tools in PATH. Wine is an execution check, not physical Windows.

The resulting own binaries passed the canonical project checker (182/182),
text decoder checks (51/51) and picture decoder checks (42/42).
The final addition builds zero-archive and zero-archive.exe from the reviewed
original source. Both match the independently built archive binaries; all
previous artifacts except the extended builder binaries remain identical.
The ISO hash is unchanged. Archive source SHA256:
780d87646a41d5d9540c60dd86bb3641c6ba3b0fc07bc71d554c6a2acf79429d

Final ISO SHA256:
c7e5903efee4b773e3b527168c7a1606fa73be9c99417cf742e3996d58137305

The native compositor reproduced kernel.zero, ezero/compiler.zero,
tools/picture.zero and media/picture-check.zero byte-for-byte from their
original Zero parts. Its Linux and Windows implementations were exercised.

Nineteen build/composition error checks passed: bad arguments, existing
output preservation, missing/invalid/oversized seeds, missing/duplicate/
unterminated markers, unknown includes, NUL source bytes, source capacity,
and injected write/fsync failures. Failed newly created artifacts were
removed, while completed earlier artifacts and existing files were preserved.

A prior self-rebuilt native builder reproduced all 37 then-existing artifacts;
a process trace showed only its initial exec and final exit. The baseline
0.11 layout was also reproduced with an external original Zero constant
variant: all 35 Linux/Windows artifacts matched and the baseline ISO matched
2c15dbc7e8f058c5ba07024c4c6c1ddd1ffcfcd86d15a2cc7c49ca7fbfd4a3df.

This report verifies compilation, reproduction and native tool tests. Guest
boot and filesystem continuation tests are documented separately. New source
revisions require their own rebuild and appropriate guest checks.

